                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Endorlight presents itself as a platformer with ambition, aiming to fuse tight movement, procedural variety, and a sense of discovery. Yet, when held up against the evergreen benchmark of excellence that is Spelunky, Endorlight falls somewhat short.  You collect money as you go down to the exit, but the system provides no meaningful, persistent payoff beyond a leaderboard ranking no one cares about.  The generated levels lack enough variety and can leave you with no reason to explore - all that matters is getting to the end of the level.\n\nFor a buck, it isn't like you will feel ripped off, but you're not going to be out there getting your friends to grab a copy so you can compete on runs.\n\nIt is a simple game, and not bad, but it is shallow and lacks an element to really motivate additional play.",
